    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "GS 27, BOS 20",
        "text": "Tatum scored Boston's first eight points, but Draymond Green hit three threes in the quarter and Golden State led 12–8 midway through and by seven after one."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "GS 44, BOS 42",
        "text": "The Warriors led 34–26 with 7:41 left before Boston closed the half on a 16–10 run. Tatum's long three in the final seconds gave him 23 first-half points and moved him past Bill Russell into eighth on the Celtics' career scoring list."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 75, GS 69",
        "text": "Mike Conley started the second half and hit two threes for Boston's first lead, 48–44, at 10:25. The Celtics built a double-digit lead late in the quarter and took 75–69 into the fourth."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: GS 88, BOS 87",
        "text": "Gui Santos hit back-to-back threes and Yaxel Lendeborg two layups to put Golden State up 81–79. Derrick White's three and a basket made it 86–83 Boston with 4:21 left, but Brandin Podziemski answered with a jumper and a 23-footer for an 88–86 lead at 2:38, the Warriors' last points. Tatum made one of two free throws with 55.6 seconds left and missed a three at 29.6; after Hugo Gonzalez stole the ball from Green, Tatum's fadeaway over Green at the horn missed."
      }
    ],
